# Exclusions for the `docker/protocol/Dockerfile` build context.
#
# Two goals:
#   1. Shrink the context upload (~1.5 GB → ~hundreds of MB) so push to the
#      buildx daemon doesn't dominate cold builds.
#   2. Stop local `forge build` / `yarn install` artifacts from invalidating
#      the forge-builder COPY layer. Without this, any local dev rebuild
#      forces forge to re-run in CI even when the underlying source is
#      untouched.
#
# Everything excluded here is regenerated inside the build (yarn install +
# forge build), or is a local-only convenience (e.g. an external
# foundry-zksync install). NOTHING source-relevant should land in this list.

# VCS / editor
.git
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Build outputs — yarn install + forge build regenerate these inside the
# container. NOTE: keep `l1-contracts/zkstack-out` (committed JSON ABIs
# consumed by `abigen!` macros at Rust compile time) — that's a different
# directory name and not matched by the patterns below.
**/node_modules
**/out
**/zkout
**/cache
**/cache-forge
**/cache-zk
**/artifacts
**/artifacts-zk
**/artifacts-forge
**/target
**/build
**/typechain
**/contracts-preprocessed
**/coverage
**/report
**/broadcast

# Local foundry install — the container uses the version installed
# from Dockerfile.base, not the host's copy.
# Local Python venv used for tooling; never referenced from the build.
venv

# Logs / temp artifacts.
**/*.log
**/yarn-error.log*
**/.lycheecache
**/UNTESTED_LINES_REPORT.md
